Maya Patel: Heads up — after the mkdocs -> docusaurus migration the sidebar TOC links on /guides/ are jumping to the top of the page instead of the section. Noticed this in Chrome and Firefox.
Jason Wu: Yikes. I think this is the slugification difference: Docusaurus strips certain chars and mkdocs/material uses a different slugify rule, so hashes no longer match.
Priya Srinivasan: Can we either normalize anchors during build or update the relative links in the docs? Which will be less work?
Linus (docs): Short term: I can add a small JS scroll-fix to detect mismatched anchor and scroll to the right element. Long term we should standardize anchor generation.
Sam (platform): Does the deploy preview show the old anchors anywhere? I saw 404s for some anchor links in the staging logs.
deploy-bot: preview-deploy/redwood-docs PR #2705 — build completed, warnings: 12 unresolved-hash-links, 3 missing anchors (guides/*.md).
Maya Patel: Thanks — Linus, if you can add the scroll-fix that'd be helpful so users aren't blocked. But let's also make a ticket to align slug rules and update links in the repo.
Jason Wu: Idea: run a small script to map old anchors to new slugs and add explicit HTML anchors where the automated slugging diverges. Example helper I used previously:
```
# python slug mapping quick script
import re
from slugify import slugify

def map_old_anchor(title):
    return slugify(title, lowercase=True, separator='-')

# then grep all links and try to match
```

Priya Srinivasan: I can take the link-updates PR for the tutorials section (mostly broken because of parentheses and colons in headings). Will submit by EOD.
Linus (docs): Quick JS patch (to add to docs/_static/scroll-fix.js) I tested locally:
```
window.addEventListener('load', () => {
  const hash = location.hash.replace('#', '');
  if (!hash) return;
  const byId = document.getElementById(hash);
  if (!byId) {
    // attempt alternate slug variants
    const alt = hash.replace(/[:()\.,]/g,'').toLowerCase();
    const el = document.querySelector(`[id^="${alt}"]`);
    if (el) el.scrollIntoView();
  }
});
```
Sam (platform): That scroll-fix is fine as a hotpatch but we should avoid JS hacks for long term. I'll open infra ticket to add slug normalization in the build pipeline.
Maya Patel: Who is owning the canonical mapping ticket?
Priya Srinivasan: I'll create the issue and the migration plan (rename/redirect list + small script to rewrite links). Assigning to @Linus for review, @Sam to prioritize in infra.
Jason Wu: For local testing, run `mkdocs serve` (or `npm run start` for docusaurus) — I found mkdocs build locally helped me iterate faster on slug heuristics.
Linus (docs): Filed PR #2712 for the JS hotpatch and a tiny test page. Running `mkdocs build` locally showed the behavior.
Maya Patel: OK set the rollout: apply JS hotpatch to staging, merge Priya's links PR into docs-next branch, then run the canonicalizer script in a single pass and open a cleanup PR.
Priya Srinivasan: PR coming: #2715 — updates tutorial links and adds a changelog entry. cc @Maya @Linus
Maya Patel: :thumbsup: thanks everyone. If anyone hits other broken anchors please drop them here or tag me.
